Q. What is load balancing? Types of load balancers in AWS?
A:	Load Balancing is the process of distributing incoming traffic evenly across multiple servers (or instances) to ensure:
High availability
Fault tolerance
Scalability
Even resource utilization
AWS provides 3 types of load balancers under the Elastic Load Balancing (ELB) service:
1. Application Load Balancer (ALB)
2. Network Load Balancer (NLB)
3. Gateway Load Balancer (GWLB)
Load Balancer Type
OSI Layer
Protocols
Use Case
Application (ALB)
Layer 7
HTTP - HyperText Transfer Protocol, HTTPS-HyperText Transfer Protocol secure
Web apps, microservices, containers
Network (NLB)
