Traffic inspection, third-party appliances


Q. What is ELB?(Elastic Load Balancer)? 
A:	Distributes incoming traffic evenly across multiple EC2 instances.

Q. What is Listener & Target Group?
A:	Listener (in ELB) checks for incoming connection requests using a specific protocol and port (e.g., HTTP on port 80, HTTPS on port 443).
it Listens for client requests & routes them based on rules to the appropriate Target Group.
Target Group is a collection of one or more backend targets (like EC2 instances, containers, Lambda functions) that will serve the requests sent by the load balancer.
Component
Purpose
Example
Listener
Listens on port/protocol (80, 443, etc.)
HTTP:80 / HTTPS:443
Target Group
Contains backend servers (targets)
EC2 instances in a target group
Rule
Matches path/host and routes to group
/api/* → API Target Group


Q. Load Balancing in AWS?
A: Load balancing Workflow: 
Internet → Load Balancer (Listener + Security Group) → Target Group → EC2 (with its Security Group)

Q. Steps to create ELB in AWS?
